A **Promise** represents a value that will be available later. `async/await` makes it read like normal code:

```javascript
async function getUser() {
  try {
    const res = await fetch("https://api.example.com/user");
    const user = await res.json();
    console.log(user);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error("Request failed:", err);
  }
}
```

`await` pauses the function until the promise resolves; errors are caught with `try/catch`.

