def bubble_sort(arr):
    n = len(arr)
    for i in range(n):
        swapped = False
        for j in range(n - 1 - i):
            if arr[j] > arr[j + 1]:
                arr[j], arr[j + 1] = arr[j + 1], arr[j]
                swapped = True
        if not swapped:
            break
    return arr

print(bubble_sort([5, 1, 4, 2]))  # [1, 2, 4, 5]
```

Each pass moves the largest remaining value to the end. It is **O(n²)**, so it is only good for learning or tiny lists.

