def find_duplicates(items):
    seen, dupes = set(), set()
    for x in items:
        if x in seen:
            dupes.add(x)
        seen.add(x)
    return list(dupes)

print(find_duplicates([1, 2, 3, 2, 1]))  # [1, 2]
```

A set gives O(1) lookups, so this runs in O(n).

